  "seoBody": "<section><span class=\"eyebrow\">New Zealand field teams</span><p>A foreman finishes a site safety walk, a plant check and a vehicle walkaround before smoko, and every answer is already filed. No app on the phone, no tablet in the ute, no paper to chase. Quickler runs the whole inspection over WhatsApp and turns it into a clean digital record the office can read the moment it lands.</p></section><h2>A morning of checks, done from one chat</h2><p>Picture a small civil or maintenance crew working across a couple of sites near Hamilton. Before any work starts there are checks to run, and most of them still live on paper or in an app nobody wants to open.</p><ul><li>A daily pre-start and site hazard sweep, signed off before the crew steps on.</li><li>A plant or harness check on the gear in use that day.</li><li>A vehicle walkaround on each ute and trailer leaving the yard.</li></ul><p>With quickler the worker opens the WhatsApp thread they already use, and the workflow asks each item in turn. They reply by text, talk into a voice note while their hands are dirty, or snap a photo of the thing in front of them. No login screen, no app update, no flat tablet battery at seven in the morning.</p><h2>One record, not a pile of forms</h2><p>Paper has to be carried, scanned and filed, and a fault written in a margin is easy to lose. Tablet apps solve some of that but add a device to issue, a login to remember and a active-user pricing for every new hire.</p><p>Quickler keeps the phone the crew already carry and puts the structure behind the chat. Each completed check becomes a live, machine-readable record on the manager dashboard, with every item marked red, amber or green so a fault on the harness or a worn tyre stands out without anyone reading line by line.</p><p>When a document is needed for a client file, a principal contractor or an auditor, a PDF exports straight from that record. The digital record is the source of truth; the PDF is just the version you can email.</p><h2>Built around the way a crew actually moves</h2><h3>Upload, do not rebuild</h3><p>Quickler is job-agnostic. Send the pre-start, plant check or vehicle walkaround you already run and it becomes a WhatsApp workflow that asks each question in order, including the conditional follow-ups for a flagged item.</p><h3>Red, amber, green at a glance</h3><p>Every answer lands on the dashboard with a status colour, and photos and voice notes sit against the item they relate to. A defect on a harness or a cracked windscreen is visible the moment it is logged, not at the end of the week.</p><h3>Town site or remote yard</h3><p>It works anywhere WhatsApp does, so a crew on a rural site reports the same way as one in the city. Data is hosted on EU servers in Germany and handled in line with GDPR, with workflows in English today and more languages on the roadmap.</p><h2>No-app inspections, answered</h2><h3>Do crews need to install anything?</h3><p>No. Everything runs over WhatsApp on the phone they already carry. No app download, no tablet to issue and only pay for active users. They answer each check by text, voice note or photo.</p><h3>Can I use my own check forms?</h3><p>Yes. Upload the daily pre-start, plant check, harness check or vehicle walkaround you already use and quickler builds it into a WhatsApp workflow that follows your order and your wording.</p><h3>What does the office receive?</h3><p>A live, structured digital record on the dashboard, with every item flagged red, amber or green. A PDF exports from that record whenever you need a document to file or send on. Read the full picture on <a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">field compliance that works anywhere</a>.</p><h3>Does it suit remote sites?</h3><p>Yes. It works wherever WhatsApp does, so spread-out crews report the same way. See the range of jobs it covers on the <a href=\"/pages/services.html\">workflows page</a>.</p>",
